Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:57:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] hw/misc: add a minimal i.MX27-style PWM model and wire it
 into the 6UL SoC
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The i.MX6UL instantiates eight independent i.MX27-style single-channel
PWM blocks (pwm1..pwm8). Up to now they were unimplemented stubs, so the
Linux pwm-imx27 driver (and the pwm-backlight consumer on our board tree)
wrote settings into a void.

Add a minimal teaching model: plain register storage for
PWMCR/PWMSR/PWMSAR/PWMPR/PWMCNR plus computed enabled/duty/period
properties so the last applied setting is observable via QMP qom-get —
that is how CI and the classroom verify 'backlight at N%' without a
waveform framework (QEMU has no PWM consumer). pwm-imx27 applies a
setting by writing SAR/PR/CR and never reads back for verification, so
storage alone makes probe and apply succeed.

Wire eight instances into fsl-imx6ul, replacing the stubs.
